WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.742 --> 00:00:01.985
(police siren)

00:00:01.985 --> 00:00:05.520
- I've been shot on the
street, stabbed in prison,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.385
been a victim of a
slashing, twice actually,

00:00:08.385 --> 00:00:09.673
dead in the morgue,

00:00:09.673 --> 00:00:12.840
died in a supermarket from overeating.

00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:16.982
My name is Ali Merhi.

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:20.552
I am an actor, and I
have played a dead body

00:00:20.552 --> 00:00:22.521
on several occasions.

00:00:22.521 --> 00:00:25.288
The director usually
tells you to hold still,

00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:27.297
try your best to hold your breath.

00:00:27.297 --> 00:00:30.232
It's good to slow your
breathing down beforehand,

00:00:30.232 --> 00:00:32.899
kind of like yoga or meditation.

00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:38.225
I played a corpse in a
morgue on Law and Order.

00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:40.025
Laying down on cold metal

00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:44.019
(laughing) while, you know, you're
practically wearing nothing,

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:47.618
it's bone chilling to say the least.

00:00:47.618 --> 00:00:49.683
You can take short breaths,

00:00:49.683 --> 00:00:52.025
but they still don't
want to see your chest

00:00:52.025 --> 00:00:53.452
going up and down at a distance.

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:54.834
They're like, "Wait a second.”

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.212
"Are you sure that guy is dead back there?”

00:00:56.212 --> 00:00:57.629
"He's breathing."

00:01:00.136 --> 00:01:02.942
Whenever you end up dying on camera,

00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:04.757
or playing dead on camera,

00:01:04.757 --> 00:01:08.920
it brings you to another emotional state.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:10.136
Normally people don't think,

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:14.388
"If I was shot or
stabbed what would I do?"

00:01:14.388 --> 00:01:16.654
But once you're there
and you're playing it,

00:01:16.654 --> 00:01:18.711
it's kind of a little traumatic.

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.504
You feel bad for people.

00:01:20.504 --> 00:01:22.571
When you see real people get hurt,

00:01:22.571 --> 00:01:24.570
you take it in a different,

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.208
you see it in a different way.

00:01:27.208 --> 00:01:29.777
My kids watch it sometimes
and they're like,

00:01:29.777 --> 00:01:31.753
"Dad, you're dead.

00:01:31.753 --> 00:01:32.610
"They killed you!"

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:36.480
I'm like, "No, I'm here
with you and I'm okay."

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.147
(gentle instrumental music)

